    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d583">

                <pb facs="0581" n="1315" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1315"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-03"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Nov. 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 660.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a copy of the
                    cipher telegram from you received November 1, and which was in response to my
                    telegram of the 30th ultimo, relating to the flagrant outrage perpetrated and
                    persisted in by the vali at Aleppo in his treatment of our consular agent at
                    that city in the case of Guedjian.</p>
                <p>I also inclose my note (copy) of this date to His Excellency Said Pasha, minister
                    of foreign affairs, which I trust you may approve.</p>
                <p>In this era of revolution and carnage some boldness in demanding not only
                    protection but respect is the only road for future security.</p>
                <pb facs="0582" n="1316" xml:id="pg1316"/>
                <p>I feel confident that in a few days proper satisfaction will be given by the
                    Porte, which will result in rendering future diplomatic action less
                    embarrassing.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



